  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday Night through Sunday)\nIssued at 1055 PM CDT Sun Oct 25 2026\n\nThe ridge begins to flatten somewhat heading into the middle part of \nthe week as the aforementioned trough lifts northeastward into the \nGreat Lakes Region on Tuesday. This could allow a few showers to \nedge into eastern Oklahoma Tuesday afternoon and evening. Overall \nrain amounts will be light as dry low level air remains in place \nover much of the region through this time. \n\nA more unsettled pattern looks to evolve through the latter part of \nthe work week into the weekend as a general breakdown of the mid \nlevel ridge still looks evident in most long range guidance. More \nsouthwesterly flow aloft along with an influx in surface moisture \nwill allow for increasing rain chances, particularly by the weekend, \nthough details will continue to be ironed out with time. There does \nnot look to be much in the way of a significant frontal passage on \nthe horizon however, meaning temperatures will continue to hold \nabove average through the period. A slight cooldown will be possible \nwith the more showery weather by the weekend.\n\nBowlan",
